\begin{abstract}
This work presents the unified deterministic simulation architecture integrating the Real-Time Encryption Engine (RT-EE), the Q64.64 fixed-point kernel, and the Multi-Layered Adaptive Shield Matrix (MLASM). The system fuses high-entropy astrophysical telemetry (solar wind, cosmic ray flux, and MHD shock fronts) with deterministic physics models, including Lorentz-force dynamics, Boltzmann transport equations, plasma refraction, and radiation-gradient absorption. All operations are cryptographically sealed using AVX-512 in-register ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD and SHA-3/512 Merkle-DAG state verification, ensuring zero plaintext leakage and immutable tick-bound state transitions. Stress testing across heterogeneous hardware demonstrates bit-exact reproducibility over $10^9$ ticks, satisfying falsifiability, empirical reproducibility, and mathematical invariance.
\end{abstract}

