\section{Methods}
\subsection{Deterministic Kernel}
The kernel operates entirely in 128-bit fixed-point representation:
\[
x \in \mathbb{Z}_{128}, \quad S_{t+1} = F(S_t),
\]
eliminating IEEE 754 drift.

Temporal determinism is enforced via the Deterministic Sequence Lock (DSL):
\[
t_{n+1} = t_n + 1,
\]
ensuring immunity to jitter.

\subsection{Real-Time Encryption Engine}
ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD is executed entirely within AVX-512 registers. Plaintext residency in RAM remains:
\[
0 \text{ bytes}.
\]

Nonce rotation is bound to tick index:
\[
N_t = t.
\]

State verification uses SHA-3/512 Merkle-DAG roots:
\[
H_t = \text{MerkleRoot}(S_t).
\]

\subsection{Astrophysical Integration}
Real NASA/ESA telemetry is normalized into Q64.64 format with zero drift. Lorentz-force dynamics:
\[
